- task_comprehensibility
- ui_response_mechanism_coherence
- lexical_accessibility
- context_naturalness
- difficulty_plausibility
- platform_deployability

For every family, judge exactly these criteria:

- plausible_format_crossing
- non_repetitive_learner_experience

For each criterion use `pass`, `minor_concern`, or `major_concern`, point to
concrete learner-visible evidence, and set `blocking` if ordinary copy-editing
would not be enough to deploy the task. Ask whether a learner would understand
what to enter or select, whether the instruction is unnecessarily technical or
verbose, whether vocabulary/context dominates the grammar practice, and
whether the interaction makes sense in a simple interface.

This is an automated product-style critique, not a user study or evidence that
any real platform would adopt the item.

